     "p": {
      "ar": "`function fee(city, weightKg = 1)` لو اتنادت من غير weightKg (أو بـ undefined) بتاخد 1. الافتراضي ممكن يكون حسبة أو حتى parameter قبله: `function price(base, vat = base * 0.14)`. ده بيشيل `if (x === undefined) x = ...` من أول كل دالة. خلي بالك: `null` مش بيشغّل الافتراضي، undefined بس.",
      "en": "`function fee(city, weightKg = 1)`: called without weightKg (or with undefined) it takes 1. A default can be a calculation, or even an earlier parameter: `function price(base, vat = base * 0.14)`. It removes `if (x === undefined) x = ...` from the top of every function. Careful: `null` does not trigger the default, only undefined."
     },
     "ex": "function shippingFee(city, weightKg = 1, express = false) {\n  const base = city === \"Cairo\" ? 40 : 60;\n  return (base + (weightKg - 1) * 10) * (express ? 1.5 : 1);\n}\nconsole.log(shippingFee(\"Cairo\"), shippingFee(\"Cairo\", 3), shippingFee(\"Giza\", 2, true));\nconsole.log(shippingFee(\"Cairo\", undefined, true), shippingFee(\"Cairo\", null));",
