      "en": "A **pure** function always gives the same result for the same inputs and changes nothing outside itself (it does not edit the array it receives, nor a global variable, nor send requests). These are the easiest functions in the world to test and understand. Keep most of your code pure (calculations and cleaning), and the «impure» parts (network, files, time) few and isolated."
